# Resolution
Fixed in commit 0243d939960c40b91920a6ff181b768948f98269
(https://github.com/justincormack/argmin/commit/0243d939960c40b91920a6ff181b768948f98269).

The Active PG metadata proof is now treated as an activation floor rather than
an immutable exact heartbeat value. Active heartbeat, active route export, PG
operation authorization, and file-backed state validation accept observations
whose applied log index has advanced beyond the peering-time proof, while still
rejecting older proofs and divergent proofs at the activation log index. This
allows normal metadata-mutating operations to advance the live storage-node
proof without breaking heartbeat lease renewal.

Regression coverage was added for accepting post-peering metadata progress,
rejecting same-index proof divergence, and loading persisted Active observations
whose metadata proof has advanced beyond the stored activation floor.

# Summary
Introduced bug: the commit adds an exact equality check between Active heartbeat proofs and the immutable peering-time proof. That is incompatible with the existing heartbeat producer, which reports live metadata state that changes during normal operation.
The new validation compares every Active PG heartbeat against pg.active_metadata_proof, which is captured once when peering completes. However, NodeHeartbeat construction reads the PG's current metadata_command_replica_state and uses the current applied_log_index, applied_log_hash, and state_digest. Normal metadata operations update those fields. As a result, after an Active PG successfully processes a metadata-changing operation such as object PUT, bucket metadata update, multipart state change, or delete marker insertion, the next storage-node heartbeat for that PG will carry a newer proof and fail PgActiveMetadataProofMismatch. The refresh loop records the error and does not install a renewed lease; once the existing heartbeat lease expires, the control plane can mark the node/PG unavailable or peering. An authenticated writer can therefore repeatedly disrupt availability in control-plane deployments by issuing normal metadata-mutating requests.

# Validation
## Rubric
- [x] Peering completion records a fixed active_metadata_proof and does not update it during later Active operation.
- [x] Active heartbeat validation compares the heartbeat metadata_proof for exact equality against that fixed proof and returns PgActiveMetadataProofMismatch on progress.
- [x] Storage-node heartbeat construction uses the current metadata_command_replica_state, not the peering-time proof.
- [x] Normal metadata command application updates applied_log_index, applied_log_hash, and state_digest, so later heartbeats can legitimately differ.
- [x] A rejected heartbeat occurs before lease renewal; repeated rejection allows the old lease to expire and forces the active PG back to Peering/unavailable.
## Report
Validated the finding as a logic/availability vulnerability. I added a focused integration PoC at crates/storage/tests/active_proof_availability_poc.rs. The PoC creates a one-node control plane, completes PG peering with PgMetadataProof(42,0xabc,0xdef), then submits an Active heartbeat with progressed proof PgMetadataProof(43,0xabd,0xdf0), modeling normal metadata-log progress. The heartbeat is rejected with ControlPlaneError::PgActiveMetadataProofMismatch, the previous lease deadline remains 2100, and expire_heartbeat_leases(2101) moves the active PG back to Peering.

Key code evidence: complete_pg_peering stores active_metadata_proof once at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:1391-1401. heartbeat calls validate_pg_heartbeat_observations before mutating/renewing lease at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:1509-1513. validate_pg_heartbeat_observations rejects any Active heartbeat whose metadata_proof differs from the stored peering proof at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:3670-3683. Storage-node heartbeats are built from current metadata_command_replica_state at crates/storage/src/node.rs:1147-1162. Metadata commands update applied_log_index/applied_log_hash/state_digest in crates/storage/src/pg_store/metadata.rs:671-693 and crates/storage/src/pg_store/command_log.rs:2540-2557. Lease expiry marks expired nodes unavailable and peering_pgs at crates/storage/src/control_plane.rs:1596-1626.

Dynamic reproduction command: CARGO_TARGET_DIR=/workspace/argmin/target-validation cargo test -p storage --test active_proof_availability_poc -- --nocapture. Output: running 1 test; test active_pg_metadata_progress_prevents_heartbeat_lease_renewal_and_expires_pg ... ok; 1 passed.

Debugger validation: lldb breakpoint at control_plane.rs:3676 stopped immediately before the mismatch return. It showed expected = PgMetadataProof { applied_log_index = 42, applied_log_hash = 2748, state_digest = 3567 } and actual observation.metadata_proof = PgMetadataProof { applied_log_index = 43, applied_log_hash = 2749, state_digest = 3568 }. Backtrace: validate_pg_heartbeat_observations -> SingleAuthorityControlPlane::heartbeat at control_plane.rs:1509 -> PoC test at active_proof_availability_poc.rs:66. This confirms the vulnerable equality check rejects normal metadata progress before lease renewal. Crash attempt was not applicable because this is not a memory-safety crash bug; the targeted debug test reproduced the availability failure. Valgrind was attempted but unavailable in the container.

